{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/483211-replacing-experience-with-freebie-points","id":483211,"title":"Replacing Experience with Freebie Points","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-16T22:52:02-07:00","id":483211,"title":"Replacing Experience with Freebie Points","content":"I've often been a little bit troubled by the long term advantages and disadvantages that come with certain distributions of attributes or powers. If you're playing a vampire, it is unwise to place 2 points into a Discipline to start out, since it would be so much more efficient in the long run to either put all 3 points into one Discipline or spread the 3 points across 3 Disciplines. The same problem exists for attributes, abilities, and other characteristics. Of course, one can always say that a player should distribute points based on character, theme, and background - but it still creates a huge temptation. The solution to this problem would be simply to eliminate Experience Points all together and give out Freebie Points at the end of every game session. Since Freebie Points go a lot further than Experience Points, the points awarded would likely be lower. Has anybody tries this or have any insights into this issue?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T00:16:06-07:00","id":483287,"title":"","content":"It works. Never done it for the cWOD, but seen it work well for Exalted (though Exalted has the primary XP sink in Charms, which have a flat cost).<br /> <br /> It might be better to take the nWOD 2e version (not exactly a big difference) which uses flat XP, which removes the biggest source of the disparity.<br /> <br /> The biggest issue if you go with pure freebies with the cWOD is that the points are that the freebie prices are purposefully imbalanced to discourage purchasing certain things; especially dots in powers. Gifts, Disciplines, Spheres, are all far more expensive in freebies than they when you compare XP rates; and they generally don't take favored traits into account.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T08:42:30-07:00","id":483569,"title":"","content":"I did this for a game of vampire, effectively having everything cost what it would to buy the second level of it. I would suggest giving out just 1 or 2 XP per session if doing this, as otherwise you get into an argument with the player who just bought Protean 3 and a single in-game week later wants to buy Protean 4 (he has 7FP, spent 5 to learn Protean 3 due to being Gangrel, and then got 3 XP points the following session).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}